<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salamanca</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Salmantica</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salamanca is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on the River <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tormes">Tormes</a>. As Salmantica it was a town of the Vettones that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> attacked in 220 BCE and later a Roman settlement on the road known as the Via de la Plata. Its university, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ix-of-leon">Alfonso IX of León</a> around 1218, is the oldest in Spain still operating and was home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/school-of-salamanca">School of Salamanca</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salamanca.jpg" alt="Salamanca" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: xiquinhosilva from Cacau · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:68436-Salamanca_(49093713952)_edited.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
